CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ int \+ long is long: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
The ranks of long and long long were derived from the width (and the
conditional operator compared types ignoring #c_type), so 1 + l was an
int where long is 32 bits, and 1ul + ll an unsigned long on LP64.
